<article class="env-lemma" id="0CDV">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CDV">Lemma <span data-tag="0CDV">29.55.6</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a scheme such that every quasi-compact open has finitely many irreducible components. Let $Z_ i \subset X$, $i \in I$ be the irreducible components of $X$ endowed with the reduced induced structure. Let $Z_ i^\nu \to Z_ i$ be the normalization. Then $\coprod _{i \in I} Z_ i^\nu \to X$ is the normalization of $X$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We may assume $X$ is reduced, see Lemma <a href="/tag/035O" data-tag="035O">29.55.2</a>. Then the lemma follows either from the local description in Lemma <a href="/tag/035P" data-tag="035P">29.55.3</a> or from Lemma <a href="/tag/035Q" data-tag="035Q">29.55.5</a> part (3) because $\coprod Z_ i \to X$ is integral and locally birational (as $X$ is reduced and has locally finitely many irreducible components). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>